      "kind": "Rule violation",
      "severity": "medium",
      "quote": "\"The hill will teach you what you need to know,\" Marcos said. \"Better than I could tell you, better than any man could. The hill does not lie about itself.\"",
      "claim": "R6 requires Marcos to answer direct curious questions 'in a STORY THAT CIRCLES the answer.' This response is a philosophical statement, not a narrative story. The boy himself notices this deviation: 'waiting for the circle that Marcos would draw, the story that would come around to the answer from the side instead of straight on. But Marcos had said his piece.'",
      "fix": "Replace with a narrative story that circles the answer, such as: 'You remember when you asked me about the river stones? I told you, go and stand by the river. The hill is the same. It will teach you what you need to know if you listen to it.'",
      "reference": "bible/R6 and bible/characters.md (Marcos section)"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "No name drift. Timeline matches Day 3 morning exactly as specified. Character traits present and consistent: [NOMBRE_ANONIMIZADO] holding and tracing the smooth stone (canonical anxiety habit), honest about fear, asking direct questions; Marcos pausing before speech, tapping stick twice before truth (R6 marker correctly deployed). Bruno's approach consistent with character. Setting details match Bible. All mysteries properly contained (M2 planted but not revealed). One medium-severity violation of form requirement in R6. Otherwise continuity-clean."
}
```

